; Comparing an account total that holds several commodities with an
; amount is an error whichever of its components Ledger meets first,
; including the order in which Ledger used to answer.
;
; Assets:Mixed received 10 EUR before it received $5.00.  Ledger used to
; compare the components one at a time and stop at the first that settled
; the answer; for this account that was the $5.00, so
; `total >= $3` listed the account and `total < $3` left it out, with no
; error, while the same comparisons on an account that had received the
; dollars first failed (value-compare-mixed-balance-error.test).  Every
; component's commodity is now checked before any is compared, so both
; comparisons fail here too, naming the euros.

2024/01/01 Euros
    Assets:Mixed     10 EUR
    Equity

2024/01/02 Dollars
    Assets:Mixed     $5.00
    Equity

test bal Assets -d 'total >= $3' -> 1
__ERROR__
While evaluating value expression:
  (total >= $3.00)
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Error: Cannot compare amounts with different commodities: 'EUR' and '$'
end test

test bal Assets -d 'total < $3' -> 1
__ERROR__
While evaluating value expression:
  (total < $3.00)
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Error: Cannot compare amounts with different commodities: 'EUR' and '$'
end test
